  "23": {
    "inputs": {
      "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>MODELS AND NODES USED IN THIS WORKFLOW</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"model-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Load Diffusion Model</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\">\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-dl\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/Winnougan/Klein9b-Distilled-Base-INT8-Convrot/resolve/main/flux-2-klein-9b-int8-convrot.safetensors\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Download flux-2-klein-9b-int8-convrot.safetensors<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnsize\\\">9.43 GB</span></a>\\n</span>&nbsp;\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><div class=\\\"pix-note-folderhint\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">Place in: ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/flux2</div><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Create the <code>flux2</code> folder if it does not exist.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"CLIP\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Load CLIP</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\">\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-dl\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-9B/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Download qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnsize\\\">8.66 GB</span></a>\\n</span>&nbsp;\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><div class=\\\"pix-note-folderhint\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">Place in: ComfyUI/models/text_encoders</div><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"VAE\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Load VAE</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\">\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-dl\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Download flux2-vae.safetensors<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnsize\\\">336 MB</span></a>\\n</span>&nbsp;\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><div class=\\\"pix-note-folderhint\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">Place in: ComfyUI/models/vae</div><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;License</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Flux 2 Klein 9B is made by Black Forest Labs and released under the <b>FLUX Non-Commercial License</b>. Read it before you use the model for paid work.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9B\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Flux 2 Klein 9B model card</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"warning-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;After placing the files, restart ComfyUI or refresh model lists using the <b>R</b> shortcut.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"nodes-installed\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Nodes Installed from Manager</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Pixaroma, version <b>1.4.183</b> or newer. A node shows red or missing? Update Pixaroma.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p><b>Which version is the newest?</b> The <b>Latest Pixaroma version</b> button shows it and what is new in it. The help page has the update steps for every kind of install.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/latest/?need=1.4.183\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Latest Pixaroma version</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/#update\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">How to update Pixaroma</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"puzzle\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something missing?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens a short video that shows the fix, with the steps written under it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/missing-nodes/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Red or missing nodes</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/missing-models/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">A model file is missing</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/refresh/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Buttons missing after an update</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"pixaroma\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Resources</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-discord\\\" href=\\\"https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Join Discord</a>&nbsp;\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-yt\\\" href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Pixaroma YouTube Channel</a>&nbsp;\\n  <span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/report/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Ask for help</a></span>&nbsp;\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Download Models\",\"icon\":\"download-model\",\"color\":\"#f66744\"}}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaInfo",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Info Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "24": {
    "inputs": {
      "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>ONE workflow that does two jobs with the same model: <b>A</b> makes a picture from text, <b>B</b> edits a picture you give it. Click A or B and press Run. No second workflow to open, no wires to move.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"to-do\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Steps</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>Click <b>A</b> on <b>Switch Source Pixaroma</b> for text to image, or <b>B</b> for an edit.</li><li>Fill in the A nodes (prompt A, size) or the B nodes (picture, prompt B).</li><li>Press <b>Run</b>.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Why Switch Source</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>A normal switch flips ONE wire. Here four wires must flip together: the prompt, the negative, the width and the height. Switch Source has rows: each row's A and B go to one output, and one click flips every row. Add rows with the <b>Rows</b> field and rename an output by clicking its name.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The same trick swaps between two models, two LoRA setups or a local and an online node: wire one setup into A, the other into B.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaInfo",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Info Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "25": {
    "inputs": {
      "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"model-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Models to download</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Orange. Each one needs a file from the <b>Download Models</b> note.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Diffusion Model (Flux 2 Klein 9B)</b> - The image model, Flux 2 Klein 9B from Black Forest Labs. It is a fast 4-step model that can make a picture from words AND change a picture you give it.</li><li><b>Load CLIP (Qwen 3 8B, reads the prompt)</b> - Reads your prompt and turns the words into something the image model understands.</li><li><b>Load VAE (Flux 2)</b> - Turns the finished render into a picture you can see, and a picture into the model's own format.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Prompt Pixaroma (A. text to image prompt)</b> - A only: describe the picture you want.</li><li><b>Sizes Pixaroma (A. picture size)</b> - A only: the picture size.</li><li><b>Load Image Mini Pixaroma (B. picture to edit)</b> - B only: the picture to edit.</li><li><b>Longest Side Pixaroma (B. work size)</b> - B only: makes the longest side 1024 and passes its size on.</li><li><b>Prompt Pixaroma (B. edit prompt)</b> - B only: say what to change in the picture.</li><li><b>Switch Source Pixaroma (1. click A or B)</b> - Flips four wires at once between two setups. Side <b>A</b> sends the text to image prompt and the Sizes size to the sampler; side <b>B</b> sends the edit (your picture + the edit prompt) and the picture's size. Click <b>A</b> or <b>B</b> on the node. Only the chosen side runs, so in A the picture is not even loaded.</li><li><b>Seed Pixaroma (2. random or fixed)</b> - The seed. <b>F</b> (fixed) gives the same result every Run, <b>R</b> (random) a new one each Run.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>CLIP Text Encode (A prompt)</b> - Reads prompt A.</li><li><b>ConditioningZeroOut (A negative)</b> - An empty negative for A.</li><li><b>CLIP Text Encode (B prompt)</b> - Reads prompt B.</li><li><b>ConditioningZeroOut (B negative)</b> - An empty negative for B.</li><li><b>VAE Encode (B picture to latent)</b> - Turns picture B into the model's format.</li><li><b>ReferenceLatent (B picture, positive)</b> - Hands picture B to Klein as the picture to edit, with prompt B.</li><li><b>ReferenceLatent (B picture, negative)</b> - The same picture, for the empty negative.</li><li><b>Empty Flux 2 Latent (blank canvas)</b> - The blank canvas, at the size the switch sends: from Sizes in A, from your picture in B.</li><li><b>KSampler (4 steps)</b> - The render: 4 steps, CFG 1, euler, simple. It gets its prompt and size from the switch.</li><li><b>VAE Decode (latent to picture)</b> - Turns the finished render into a picture.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Preview Image Pixaroma (the picture, saved)</b> - Shows the picture and saves it into <code>ComfyUI/output/Two Jobs</code>.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaInfo",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Info Pixaroma"
    }
  },
  "26": {
    "inputs": {
      "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>RUN TIMES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Measured on a <b>24 GB RTX 4090</b> with this workflow, with the models already loaded. A different card gives different numbers, but the shape holds: the time grows with the number of pictures and their size.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Size</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A: text to image</td><td>1024 x 1024</td><td>about 1.8 s</td></tr><tr><td>B: edit</td><td>1024 x 1024</td><td>about 3 s</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"warning-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The first Run of the session</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The first Run after starting ComfyUI also has to load the models from disk (about 18 GB for Klein and its text encoder), so it takes longer. After that they stay loaded.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"run-timer\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;On a 16 GB card</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Timed on an <b>RTX 4060 Ti 16 GB</b> with 32 GB of RAM:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Klein took about <b>3 to 6 times</b> as long, about 10 s even for one picture: Klein and its text encoder (17 GB together) do not fit in 16 GB, so parts of them load again on every Run, and a second Run is no faster.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Run Times\",\"icon\":\"run-timer\",\"color\":\"#3f9a4f\"}}"
    },
    "class_type": "PixaromaInfo",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Info Pixaroma"
    }
  },
